4. ASIs / Professional Development Proficiency Codes (PDPCs) associated with CMF 18 SGM/CSM: 6C Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6K Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 6P Post Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6S Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Experience 6U Post Battalion Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 6X Post Brigade Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 7C Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 7K Primary Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 7P Post Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience', 'c04fef49c87c4c370f3b71a052c2cace5704232b4d96246849607e6b237dc0d1', 21, 22, null, 51, null, null, false, null),
  ('ec06b79b-7244-5bc8-a16b-a938f92ab482', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Special Forces branch guidance is for Noncommissioned Officers to serve in Key Development positions to be considered minimally MOS qualified (MMQ). SF NCOs should serve in a variety of institutional and operational billets throughout their career to increase their development. Professional Development Models for MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z are available at https://actnow.army.mil; and on the Army HRC website at https://www.hrc.army.mil/content/CMF%2018%20Information. NOTE: Proponent guidance should not be construed as a simplified checklist for promotion selection. It does not guarantee promotion or a competitive Order of Merit (OML) number following the Evaluation Boards. NCOs who have completed assignments in Key Development positions and consistently outperformed their peers with supporting rater and senior rater comments are viewed more favorably by board members.', 'd9b38e3ce8e2986a030eb301a72203b91af801f0d5dc60b159e736da156a01be', 11, 11, null, 52, null, null, false, null),
  ('276b6854-d815-5d7a-8f07-ff6f75e29e12', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — There are no authorized CMF 18 Sergeant positions in the Regiment', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'All Soldiers who graduate the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC) and meet the requirements outlined in AR 600- 8- 19: Chapter 3-1 para. (a) Regular Army will be promoted to the rank of Sergeant. These Sergeants will fill Staff Sergeant positions and follow the career path of Staff Sergeants as outlined below. NOTE: In accordance with the exception to policy from USAJFKSWCS to the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff, G1 to current promotion policy AR 600-8-19 authorizes automatic promotion to Sergeant without regard to TIG or TIS, an appearance to a decentralized promotion board effective upon graduation from the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC). A Soldier who is otherwise qualified in accordance with paragraphs 1–11. Non- promotable status, AR 600-8- 19, one rank up to the rank of SGT.', 'baa12fb028573d34b62970c7d7e4b89dde129452377920ec433e0a2c0a83ef21', 12, 12, null, 53, null, null, false, null),
  ('ea2359c9-ad5a-57c2-af34-8ded31b36578', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Must be a Basic Leader Course Graduate.', 'bc3706c896b99304d932b16572f09ae95c80869edbadfef92c2338d34a4e37b1', 12, 12, null, 54, null, null, false, null),
  ('45e4a99d-d03d-53d6-8831-55be22244202', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B3, 18C3, 18D3, 18E3 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, and Communications Sergeants CMF18 Staff Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “6H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SSG will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'ab61e8eca78a09a05ac50fd72d4df8153a945f57fbf6fb1acdc39af58189f046', 13, 13, null, 55, null, null, false, null),
  ('8d90870c-95b3-53a0-9683-da67915c4158', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38; and rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
